diff --git a/docs/upgrading.rst b/docs/upgrading.rst
index caa56c1b..8edc2127 100644
--- a/docs/upgrading.rst
+++ b/docs/upgrading.rst
@@ -6,6 +6,39 @@ This section documents migration paths to new releases.
 Upgrading to 3.26
 +++++++++++++++++
 
+Schema-level validator errors are keyed by ``data_key``
+*******************************************************
+
+Errors reported by a `validates_schema <marshmallow.validates_schema>` method for a
+specific field are now keyed by that field's ``data_key``, if it has one. This makes
+them consistent with errors raised by fields and by
+`validates <marshmallow.validates>` methods, which have always used ``data_key``.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from marshmallow import Schema, ValidationError, fields, validates_schema
+
+
+    class MySchema(Schema):
+        ip_addresses = fields.String(data_key="ipAddresses")
+
+        @validates_schema
+        def validate_ip_addresses(self, data, **kwargs):
+            raise ValidationError("Invalid IP addresses.", "ip_addresses")
+
+
+    # <3.26
+    MySchema().validate({"ipAddresses": "invalid"})
+    # {'ip_addresses': ['Invalid IP addresses.']}
+
+    # >=3.26
+    MySchema().validate({"ipAddresses": "invalid"})
+    # {'ipAddresses': ['Invalid IP addresses.']}
+
+Note that the argument passed to `ValidationError <marshmallow.exceptions.ValidationError>`
+(or used as a key in its error dict) is still the *field name*, not the ``data_key``.
+Only the key of the resulting error message changes.
+
 ``ordered`` is deprecated
 *************************
 
